      <div type="clause" n="45.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 45.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="xno" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="518" ed="#liebermann"/>E [s]e<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_45-1.lnote.oe.1"/> hum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_45-1.lnote.oe.2"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_45-1.lnote.oe.a"/> le chalange, e il n’en<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#LeisWl_45-1.lnote.oe.3"/> ait testimonie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#LeisWl_45-1.lnote.oe.4"/>, si n’ad nul warant, rende l’um<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#LeisWl_45-1.lnote.oe.5"/> a l’hum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#LeisWl_45-1.lnote.oe.6"/> soun chatel; e le forfait ait<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#LeisWl_45-1.lnote.oe.7"/> qui<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#LeisWl_45-1.lnote.oe.8"/> aver le deit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="518" ed="#liebermann"/>Quodsi aliquis rem postmodum calumpniatus fuerit, et nec testes habuerit nec warantum, et rem reddat, et forisfacturam cui de iure competit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="45.1" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="272" ed="#robertson"/>E [s]e hum le chalange e il n'en ait testimonie, si n'ad nul warant, rende l'um a l'hum soun chatel, e le forfait ait qui aver le deit.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="518" ed="#liebermann"/>45, 1. Und wenn jemand es<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_45-1.lnote.de1.a"/> (nachher <hi rend="italic">L</hi>) beansprucht, und [Besitz]er hat kein [Kauf-]Zeugniss darüber und er hat [auch] keinen Gewährsmann<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_45-1.lnote.de.1"/>, so gebe er jenem [Kläger] dessen Werthstück zurück<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_45-1.lnote.de1.b"/>: und das Strafgeld empfange, wer es zu empfangen berechtigt ist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">45, 1. And if someone (afterwards <hi rend="italic">L</hi>) claims it, and the [possess]or has no [purchase-]testimony about it and he has [also] no warrantor, then he shall give back to that [plaintiff] his article of value: and let him receive the money penalty who is entitled to receive it.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="273" ed="#robertson"/>And if anyone claims it and he has no witnesses and no warrantor, the goods shall be given up to the claimant, and the fine shall be paid to the party who is entitled thereto.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="518"><ref target="clause:IICn_24-1">II Cn 24.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">II Cn. 24, 1</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 272–273 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 518, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_45-1.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">518</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> puis <hi rend="italic">aus L Cnut</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply puis from L Cnut</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_45-1.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">518</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">le <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">le I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_45-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">518</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">lum <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lum Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_45-1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">518</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">vent <hi rend="italic">Io;</hi> nen <hi rend="italic">MA.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">vent Io; nen MA.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_45-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">518</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">testem. <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">testem. Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_45-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">518</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">lun <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lun Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_45-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">518</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">lun son <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lun son Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_45-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">518</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eit <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eit Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_45-1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">518</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ki <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ki Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_45-1.lnote.de1.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">518</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nicht</hi> ihn, <hi rend="italic">laut L und Cnut</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">not ‘him’, according to L and Cnut</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_45-1.lnote.de1.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">518</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt</hi> æftergeld; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Cnut u. o.</hi> 21, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æftergeld is missing; cf. Cnut and above 21, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_45-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">292</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Vielleicht bewusst von Cnut abweichend, gemäss <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. 21{4}; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Anefang 4A. 12</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Perhaps deliberately departing from Cnut, in accordance with <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 21{4}; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Anefang 4A. 12</seg></note>
      </div>
